{"name":"September Song","hex":"#d5d8c8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"song","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical composition with lyrics for voice or voices, performed by singing.","Any musical composition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/song"}],"entries":[{"title":"September Song","blocks":[{"text":"\"September Song\" is an American standard popular song composed by Kurt Weill with lyrics by Maxwell Anderson. It was introduced by Walter Huston in the 1938 Broadway musical production Knickerbocker Holiday. The song has been recorded by numerous singers and instrumentalists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September_Song","wikidata":"Q7452233"},{"title":"September Song (JP Cooper song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"September Song\" is a song by English singer JP Cooper. It is the second single from his debut studio album, Raised Under Grey Skies (2017). The song was released as a digital download in the United Kingdom on 16 September 2016 through Island Records. The song has peaked at number 7 on the UK Singles Chart, and has also reached the top 10 in both Ireland and Sweden. The song was written by Cooper, Jon Hume, Alex Bunker and Mr Hudson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/JP_Cooper_-_September_Song.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September_Song_(JP_Cooper_song)","wikidata":"Q62063176"},{"title":"September","blocks":[{"text":"September is the ninth month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 30 days."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_septembre.jpg/330px-Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_septembre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September","wikidata":"Q123"},{"title":"Song","blocks":[{"text":"A song is a musical composition performed by the human voice. The voice often carries the melody using patterns of sound and silence. Songs have a structure, such as the common ABA form, and are usually made of sections that are repeated or performed with variation later. A song without instruments is said to be a cappella."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Billie_Holiday%2C_Downbeat%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_ca._Feb._1947_%28William_P._Gottlieb_04251%29.jpg/330px-Billie_Holiday%2C_Downbeat%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_ca._Feb._1947_%28William_P._Gottlieb_04251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song","wikidata":"Q7366"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/Nadine_Coyle_-_September_Song_artwork.jpg/250px-Nadine_Coyle_-_September_Song_artwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/78/Nadine_Coyle_-_September_Song_artwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/Nadine_Coyle_-_September_Song_artwork.jpg/250px-Nadine_Coyle_-_September_Song_artwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANadine_Coyle_-_September_Song_artwork.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Sapphire_ring.jpg/500px-Sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Sapphire_ring.jpg/1280px-Sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Sapphire_ring.jpg/500px-Sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"